# Chunks — Memory Drill

## Purpose

Drill high-frequency phrases as atomic units. Do not decompose into grammar. Prompt with English → produce full Greek phrase from memory.

Timing is the learner's 4 / 6 / 8 s choice plus 35% for each extra word in the answer
(`src/routes/practice/components/drill-speeds.ts`), so longer phrases get more time automatically.

## Implemented set — 24 items in `chunks.tsx`

Three categories, filterable in the drill: Social (11) · Survival (5) · Starters (8).

### Social (`category: "social"`)
| English | Greek |
|---------|-------|
| Hello / Hi | Γεια σου |
| Hello (formal) | Γεια σας |
| Good morning | Καλημέρα |
| Good evening | Καλησπέρα |
| Good night | Καληνύχτα |
| Goodbye | Αντίο |
| See you later | Τα λέμε |
| Thank you | Ευχαριστώ |
| Please / You're welcome | Παρακαλώ |
| Excuse me / Sorry | Συγγνώμη |
| How are you? | Τι κάνεις; |

Informal and formal greeting are **separate items** (`hello` / `hello-formal`), not one item with
two accepted answers.

### Survival (`category: "survival"`)
| English | Greek |
|---------|-------|
| I don't understand | Δεν καταλαβαίνω |
| I don't know | Δεν ξέρω |
| Can you speak more slowly? | Μπορείτε να μιλάτε πιο αργά; |
| How do you say...? | Πώς λέγεται; |
| What does ... mean? | Τι σημαίνει; |

### Starters (`category: "starters"`) — frames, not full sentences
| English prompt | Greek opener |
|----------------|--------------|
| My name is... (opener) | Με λένε |
| I would like... (opener) | Θα ήθελα |
| Where is...? | Πού είναι; |
| How much is...? | Πόσο κάνει; |
| Can I... (opener) | Μπορώ να |
| I need to... (opener) | Πρέπει να |
| I want to... (opener) | Θέλω να |
| Do you have...? | Έχετε; |

### Punctuation

Drill `greek` strings keep the authentic Greek question mark (`Τι κάνεις;`). `phoneticEquals` in
`src/lib/greek-transliteration.ts` strips terminal punctuation from both sides, so the learner is
never required to type it. Do not strip `;` from content to make a card passable.

### Not implemented

`Είμαι καλά` ("I'm fine") is a natural pair for `Τι κάνεις` but is not in the item list. Add it to
`chunks.tsx` and update the subtitle count if it is wanted.

## Drill format

**Forward**: English prompt → type the Greek phrase in greeklish
**Reverse**: Greek phrase → English, self-assess

No paradigm table. No person/number selector. Pure sequential recall.
Colour theme: honey. Returns to `/practice/blocks`.

## Build order

Social (11) → Survival (5) → Starters (8). Drill Social to automaticity before moving on; Starters
are lowest priority, as the learner may already have them from tutor work.

## Notes

- Sentence starters are frames — drill just the opener chunk ("Θα ήθελα"), not a full sentence
- Γεια is not seeded as an alternative to Αντίο; if a variant is wanted, use `acceptAlso`
- There is no `greeklish` field: it is derived, never stored. The typed answer is graded by
  `matchPhonetic` against `greek`, and feedback shows the Greek with its derived pronunciation
  (`<GreekGloss>`). Συγγνώμη is said [siɣnomi], so "signomi" must pass; if a card is unpassable,
  fix the matcher, never the content
- If learner's tutor work has covered these already, this drill surfaces which are NOT yet automatic vs which can be deprioritised
